    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is positioned for a high-ceiling performance today, spearheaded by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 score makes him our premier start. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a potent combination of a 4.60 xERA matchup against Luis Severino and an elite +15% SP skill adjustment. Furthermore, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.99) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.88) round out the top tier of our lineup. **Jacob Wilson** is particularly intriguing, as a significant +16% park factor adjustment elevates his utility, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** exploits a favorable platoon advantage against Sandy Alcantara. We are also closely tracking **Brady House** (60.52); while his base projection is modest, the combination of Alcantara\u2019s slow delivery to the plate and a strong platoon edge makes him a high-leverage target for stolen base opportunities, which remain our critical scarcity focus.\n\nThe toughest call of the morning involved **Nasim Nunez**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a 55.82 score. While **Nasim Nunez** gained a 4% efficiency boost from the exploitable battery matchup against Alcantara, his bottom-of-the-order positioning (-8%) ultimately forced him to the bench in favor of the higher-projected **Josh Jung** and **Heliot Ramos**. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Sam Antonacci** (43.60) and **Heliot Ramos** (48.39); both face difficult matchups against Logan Gilbert and Chandler respectively, with the low SP xERA marks for those starters dampening their overall projections. While **Luis Robert Jr.** remains on the IL, the depth of the squad ensures we have enough volume to weather these tougher matchups without sacrificing our aggressive stance on speed and efficiency.",
